    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37067" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏpŭliscītum</span></b> ,
			i, n., or better written separately, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pŏpŭli
			scītum</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a decree of the people</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Athenienses nihil nisi populi scitis ac
					decretis agebant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 1, 27, 43</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Opt. Gen. 7, 19</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populiscito in patriam restitutus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Arist. 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scitum populi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					45, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
